+# Transfer time
+
+Locally enabled **untrusted Python**. This extension has no upstream admission,
+no fresh held-out admission, and no formal proof. Its source and tests are new
+packaging inputs; historical release/admission hashes are not rewritten.
+The U1 Workbench replay verdict belongs to different source and is not inherited.
+
+Ask `How long does it take to transfer 1GB at100Mbps?` for **80 seconds**, explicitly
+labelled an ideal estimate at 100% utilization, without startup delay. Add
+`with 80% utilization` to estimate throughput losses. Actual transfer time can
+be longer. This does not read files, measure networks, or access private state.
+
+Use `How long does it take to`, `How long to`, or `How many seconds to`, followed
+by `transfer`, `download`, or `upload`. Give one size, `at` and one sustained rate
+(or `over a RATE connection`), and optionally utilization. Extra conditions such
+as changing rates and startup delay are refused, not silently ignored.
+
+B means bytes and b means bits. Size units: B, kB, MB, GB, TB, KiB, MiB, GiB, TiB.
+Rates: bps, kbps, Mbps, Gbps, Tbps, or a size unit followed by /s. Unit spelling is
+case-sensitive. Decimal prefixes use powers of 1000; binary powers of 1024.
+Size may be zero; rate must be positive; utilization must be in (0,100].
+Inputs are bounded to 4096 characters and 18 integer plus 12 fractional digits
+per number. Fractions are exact before display rounding to 12 significant digits.
+
+The existing combiner loads the manifest through `standing_extensions_v1.txt`.
+w554 consults these local extensions only after core/star/owner answers, only on
+eligible reading declines, preserving privacy, precision and terminal guards.
+Ordinary replies carry qualification in provenance. Direct operation discovery
+uses the same standing registration and exposes source qualification; direct
+results include it too. Direct calls bypass the head's global guards and are
+labelled accordingly by the operations adapter.
+
+`panel.json` contains fresh development/domain controls, with independently
+written literal expected results. Its held-out list is empty: no new admission
+exam is represented. A full candidate Engine check remains an integration step;
+component tests do not pretend to run the complete Engine.
